<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso XII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso XII was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from 1874 to 1885. Son of Isabella II, he was proclaimed king by a military coup in December 1874, ending the First Republic and beginning the Restoration. His reign brought the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-carlist-war">Third Carlist War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, and the constitution of 1876.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii.jpg" alt="Alfonso XII" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando Debás · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfons_XII_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Alfonso was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a> on 28 November 1857, the eldest son of Queen Isabella II. His official father, her husband Francisco de Asís, was generally viewed as effeminate, impotent or homosexual, which led writers to question Alfonso's paternity. When the Revolution of 1868 forced Isabella to leave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, he went with her to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and was sent to study at the Theresianum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. On 25 June 1870 his mother abdicated in his favour in Paris.</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> chose Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeo-i-of-spain">Amadeo of Savoy</a> as king in November 1870, but he abdicated in early 1873 after attacks on his life and the outbreak of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-carlist-war">Third Carlist War</a>. The First Spanish Republic followed, facing war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, uprisings in Spanish Morocco and the Carlist rising. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-canovas-del-castillo">Antonio Cánovas del Castillo</a> led a group favouring a Bourbon Restoration and took charge of Alfonso's education, sending him to the Royal Military College, Sandhurst.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>On 1 December 1874 Alfonso issued the Sandhurst Manifesto, which set out the ideological basis of the Restoration and proclaimed him the sole representative of the Spanish monarchy. At the end of 1874 Brigadier Martínez Campos led battalions to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagunto">Sagunto</a>, rallied the troops sent against him and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> in the king's name. The republic's president resigned and power passed to Cánovas. Alfonso was proclaimed king on 29 December 1874. In 1876 a campaign against the Carlists, in which he took part, ended with the defeat of Don Carlos.</p><p>Cánovas was the real architect of the Restoration, which proved a civilian regime lasting until Primo de Rivera's coup in 1923. The Constitution of 1876 and the Pact of El Pardo of 1885 endorsed turnismo, the alternation of conservative and liberal prime ministers. In 1881 Alfonso refused to sanction a law fixing ministers' terms at 18 months, and when Cánovas resigned he called the Liberal leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/praxedes-mateo-sagasta">Práxedes Mateo Sagasta</a> to form a government.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Alfonso died on 25 November 1885, aged 27, at the Royal Palace of El Pardo near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>. He had tuberculosis, but the immediate cause of death was a recurrence of dysentery. His widow, pregnant, became regent, and their son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xiii">Alfonso XIII</a> was born in 1886. Alfonso had won popular affection by visiting districts struck by cholera and by the Andalusian earthquake of 1884. His reign is credited with ending the political instability of the previous decades, and a monument to him by José Grases Riera was completed in the Parque del Buen Retiro in Madrid in 1922.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Alfonso XII” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In December 1874 General Arsenio Martínez Campos proclaimed <b>Alfonso XII</b>, son of Isabella II, at Sagunto, ending the Sexenio Democrático.</blockquote><a href="/state/restoration-spain">Restoration Spain</a></li><li><blockquote>In December 1874 General Martínez Campos proclaimed <b>Alfonso XII</b> at Sagunto, opening Restoration Spain.</blockquote><a href="/state/sexenio-democratico">Sexenio Democrático</a></li><li><blockquote>A unitary republic under Serrano followed until General Martínez Campos proclaimed <b>Alfonso XII</b> in December 1874, beginning Restoration Spain.</blockquote><a href="/state/spanish-first-republic">Spanish First Republic</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Royal Palace of Madrid, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in Royal Palace of El Pardo, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.42,-3.71&amp;year=1875" aria-label="Royal Palace of Madrid on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of Alfonso XII"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n30.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4758 4110h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4758 4110h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=40.42,-3.71&amp;year=1875">What was here in 1875? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
